### TRAP A: does 'read < /proc/file' return the whole value?
DISTRO       bin_sh     read_builtin   cat_version    stat_size  verdict
arch         bash       4194304        4194304        0          read builtin gives the SAME answer as cat (safe here)
ubuntu2404   dash       4              4194304        0          read builtin TRUNCATES procfs data (must use cat)
debian13     dash       4              4194304        0          read builtin TRUNCATES procfs data (must use cat)
fedora42     bash       4194304        4194304        0          read builtin gives the SAME answer as cat (safe here)

### TRAP B: set -o pipefail
DISTRO       accepts      effect                 detail
arch         yes          exit 1 (1 means pipefail is real) [pipefail       	on]
ubuntu2404   NO           exit 0 (0 = last command wins) /bin/sh: 1: set: Illegal option -o pipefail
debian13     yes          exit 1 (1 means pipefail is real) [pipefail        on]
fedora42     yes          exit 1 (1 means pipefail is real) [pipefail       	on]

